<newsitem itemid="385700" id="root" date="1997-02-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: Conseco Inc Q4 oper net rises.</title>
<headline>Conseco Inc Q4 oper net rises.</headline>
<dateline>CARMEL, Ind. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr primary	 $0.54		    $0.43</p>
<p> Oper shr diluted	 $0.54		    $0.40</p>
<p> Oper net		  85,700		   42,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     159,600		   86,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     160,500		  104,500</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: Including investment gains or losses, restructuring income and restructuring charges, net income in Q4 was $77.9 million, or $0.49 a diluted share, compared with net income of $52.6 million, or $0.50 a share a year ago. Including those factors, net income was $0.49 a primary share, vs $0.55 a primary share a year ago.  </p>
<p>		 Year</p>
<p>				 1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr primary		$1.91		    $2.34</p>
<p> Oper shr diluted		$1.89		     1.26</p>
<p> Oper net			252,400		  220,400</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	    126,800		   86,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	    142,500		  104,500</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Weighted average shares for calculating diluted earnings per share increased because of the company's August purchase of Life Partners Group and its January 1996 offering of PRIDES, which are manditorily convertible into Conseco common stock.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
